1
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,430
[BORAQCHIN]
The House of Tolui is in ruins.

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,640
[♪ drum beats]

3
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,030
[wind blowing]

4
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:24,860
[BORAQCHIN] Uh?

5
00:00:25,530 --> 00:00:26,820
♪

6
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:35,380
Oh, it disappeared.

7
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:37,630
[laughs]

8
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:40,510
[MÖGE] Boraqchin!
So this is where you are!

9
00:00:40,590 --> 00:00:41,590
[BORAQCHIN] Hmm?

10
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:44,130
They've got all manner
of gemstones over there.

11
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,590
-Let's go look!
-Gemstones?

12
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,260
Yes! I hear
it's a caravan of traders

13
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:51,850
that returned from the west.
Come on already!

14
00:00:51,930 --> 00:00:55,230
Wait a moment.
I'm afraid that gemstones

15
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:57,440
wouldn't look very flattering
on someone like me.

16
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:58,610
[MÖGE] Mm?

17
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,820
-[MÖGE] So what?
-Uh?

18
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,320
It can be plenty of fun
just to look around.

19
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,360
-[Möge chuckles]
-[BORAQCHIN] Uh...

20
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:13,870
Hurry up! [chuckles]

21
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:15,080
♪

22
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:27,260
[Kirgistani exclaims]

23
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:30,220
[Boraqchin gasps]

24
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,640
[MÖGE] Look at these.

25
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,020
Don't you think
that we could make

26
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,940
some lovely earrings
out of them?

27
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,940
Yes, they're splendid.

28
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,980
You should try to find something
for yourself, too.

29
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,730
Oh, no, not for me.

30
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:45,280
[Möge exclaims]

31
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:53,870
[Boraqchin gasps]

32
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:58,710
[MAN] I wouldn't bother
with that stone if I were you.

33
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:00,880
That one somehow
found its way

34
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,750
into the batch of gemstones
we recently procured.

35
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,760
It's honestly a meddlesome stone

36
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,970
that crumbles
whenever it's exposed to light.

37
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:10,260
Crumbles? In the light?

38
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:13,560
As if by fate,

39
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:15,600
I discovered
this shabby-looking rock

40
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,810
amidst the dazzling gemstones,

41
00:02:17,890 --> 00:02:20,940
and found myself
strangely fascinated by it.

42
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,570
A simple stone.
That was how it all began.

43
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:29,950
[♪ opening theme song playing]

44
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,050
[BORAQCHIN] Uh?

45
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:12,340
It's coated in a powder.

46
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,050
[sighs]

47
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:20,390
This hard stone is already
beginning to wear away

48
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,310
in a few days of sunlight.

49
00:04:23,350 --> 00:04:25,060
How curious.

50
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:27,310
♪

51
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:29,480
After reading up on it,

52
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:31,740
I learned this stone
was called sandarac

53
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:34,990
and was known in the east
for its medicinal properties.

54
00:04:35,950 --> 00:04:37,660
Taken in appropriate doses,

55
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:40,700
it could heal abscesses
and restore one's vigor.

56
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,750
However, when heated
over a fire,

57
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:46,750
it turns into a white substance
known as arsenic...

58
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:50,630
A deadly poison
that dissolves in water

59
00:04:50,710 --> 00:04:53,050
and is devoid of taste or odor.

60
00:04:53,670 --> 00:04:56,760
This brittle rock
unfit to be a gemstone.

61
00:04:56,840 --> 00:05:00,560
It's just...
It's just so fascinating.

62
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:05,520
In the following year,
Genghis Khan met his demise.

63
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:07,560
As his consorts,

64
00:05:07,650 --> 00:05:09,730
Möge and I were uncertain
of our fate,

65
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:13,440
but ended up being taken
as wives by our stepson Ögedei.

66
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:15,030
And I...

67
00:05:15,650 --> 00:05:19,320
Somehow became
Ögedei's primary empress.

68
00:05:20,490 --> 00:05:23,330
Why did he choose me?

69
00:05:23,910 --> 00:05:27,330
I thought it was simply
because I was the eldest.

70
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:28,540
But...

71
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:31,840
Wow! A rock that crumbles
in the light?

72
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,800
[BORAQCHIN]
A trifling hobby of mine.

73
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,680
Please pay it no mind.

74
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,800
Very well. It does seem
beyond my understanding.

75
00:05:40,470 --> 00:05:44,430
That said, I am happy to learn
about something you enjoy.

76
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,730
Please let me know

77
00:05:45,810 --> 00:05:47,600
if there are any other rocks
you would want.

78
00:05:47,690 --> 00:05:49,060
I'll make sure you get them.

79
00:05:49,150 --> 00:05:53,150
Yes. But...
why do so much for me?

80
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,700
[ÖGEDEI] The desire
to obtain something...

81
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:01,580
That is the urge that sets
the world in motion.

82
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:02,990
[Boraqchin gasps softly]

83
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,200
♪

84
00:06:05,950 --> 00:06:07,500
I have my own desire.

85
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:09,920
that this steppe will someday
be a vast market

86
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,630
that connects east and west.

87
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,500
Can you see it?

88
00:06:13,590 --> 00:06:15,590
Eastern and western
cultures alike

89
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:17,130
passing through to do trade.

90
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:19,260
In such a world,

91
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:22,220
we won't need to venture off
to wage war and plunder.

92
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:24,930
People and goods
will gather here willingly.

93
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,480
[Boraqchin gasps softly]

94
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,770
Thanks for your offer.

95
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:32,020
I'm really looking
for more books.

96
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:35,070
I want to learn about the nature
of these stones.

97
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:36,860
Very well then.

98
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:40,110
I'm truly glad
you're my empress.

99
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,780
Thank you for accepting.

100
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:45,370
Tolui and the others
would never understand

101
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:47,500
what I hope to accomplish.

102
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:49,500
That's why
I want someone like you

103
00:06:49,580 --> 00:06:52,040
who can truly
appreciate it by my side.

104
00:06:52,130 --> 00:06:53,920
[Boraqchin gasps softly]

105
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,300
♪

106
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,550
[BORAQCHIN]
The House of Tolui's power

107
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:02,760
will inhibit him
from acting freely.

108
00:07:03,550 --> 00:07:06,140
Can nothing be done about that?

109
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,640
Empress Boraqchin...

110
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:10,980
Your new physician is here
to see you.

111
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,900
-[Möge chuckles]
-And Lady Möge as well.

112
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,400
Hello!

113
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:16,980
[PHYSICIAN] Oh, my goodness.

114
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:18,690
[BORAQCHIN]
I'm quite fond of rocks

115
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:20,450
that change
appearance and behavior

116
00:07:20,530 --> 00:07:22,160
under heat or light.

117
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:25,330
Eastern physicians
like yourself are well-versed

118
00:07:25,410 --> 00:07:27,120
in such matters, am I correct?

119
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,870
Indeed.

120
00:07:36,170 --> 00:07:37,250
[Möge breathes softly]

121
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:39,260
[PHYSICIAN] By any chance,
have you heard

122
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:41,800
of the Daoist doctrine
known as waidan?

123
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,260
I'm not familiar.

124
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:46,140
Using fire or water
to refine stones

125
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:47,470
like these ones,

126
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:50,230
they tried to concoct elixirs
of immortality.

127
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:54,770
But inaccurate methods resulted
in a deadly poison instead.

128
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,820
[BORAQCHIN]
It was at this moment

129
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:59,940
that a plot began
to formulate in my mind.

130
00:08:08,290 --> 00:08:11,290
The physician told me
if I heated this powder,

131
00:08:11,370 --> 00:08:13,460
it would give me arsenic.

132
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:16,210
Which is lethal in minute doses.

133
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,500
In its sandarac form,

134
00:08:19,590 --> 00:08:21,380
this shouldn't be enough
to kill.

135
00:08:22,430 --> 00:08:24,800
Unlike arsenic,
this doesn't even dissolve

136
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,180
when mixed in water.

137
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:29,010
Such a truly ungraceful stone.

138
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:33,350
In that sense, you could say
it is just like me.

139
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:35,600
♪

140
00:08:39,230 --> 00:08:40,940
[Boraqchin coughing]

141
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:48,830
I see.

142
00:08:48,910 --> 00:08:51,790
That dose is enough
to cause this?

143
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:53,790
Now, all that remains...

144
00:08:54,410 --> 00:08:56,540
is to find what cures it.

145
00:08:56,630 --> 00:08:58,710
Sandarac poison leaves the body

146
00:08:58,790 --> 00:09:01,420
after three months
of recuperation.

147
00:09:02,130 --> 00:09:03,800
But was there no faster,

148
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:06,510
more dramatic remedy
I could use?

149
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:08,970
One that would seem
like a miracle?

150
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:14,730
That was my question
when I finally met that girl.

151
00:09:15,390 --> 00:09:16,600
♪

152
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:28,370
[BORAQCHIN] What do I do?

153
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:31,080
One false move,
and this plan will put

154
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:33,500
the Great Kha'an's life
in peril.

155
00:09:35,710 --> 00:09:36,870
[Boraqchin exhales]

156
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,960
[chuckles]

157
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:42,670
[laughing]

158
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:47,050
Obviously, I should
entrust all of our fates

159
00:09:47,130 --> 00:09:48,930
into the hands of Tengri,
shouldn't I?

160
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:55,600
A divination!
We must perform one at once!

161
00:09:58,390 --> 00:09:59,730
[birds chirping]

162
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,400
[SLAVE] Huh?

163
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:05,950
Here will do.

164
00:10:12,950 --> 00:10:14,540
So is everything prepared?

165
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:17,710
Oh, well, divinations require
sheep bones,

166
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:19,040
but we don't have any.

167
00:10:19,130 --> 00:10:21,460
The fire isn't to heat up bones.

168
00:10:22,710 --> 00:10:23,670
[SLAVE] Huh?

169
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:27,880
Listen well. Cover your nose
and mouth with a cloth.

170
00:10:27,970 --> 00:10:29,630
And don't stand downwind
of the fire.

171
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,640
[SLAVE] Uh?

172
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:35,640
[BORAQCHIN] Did you not hear me?
Cover yourself at once.

173
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,930
[SLAVE] Oh, right.

174
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:49,070
[SLAVE] The red powder
is turning white in the fire?

175
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:50,200
[gasps]

176
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,580
A good omen.

177
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,240
[slave breathes shakily]

178
00:10:54,870 --> 00:10:56,040
[BORAQCHIN] Sure enough.

179
00:10:56,330 --> 00:10:59,460
From there, everything proceeded
exactly as planned.

180
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:00,960
♪

181
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:07,800
[inhales]

182
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:10,970
[Boraqchin exhales]

183
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:14,600
Yes, all as planned.

184
00:11:15,050 --> 00:11:16,510
-[MÖGE] Boraqchin?
-Uh?

185
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:19,180
The Great Kha'an is here.

186
00:11:21,270 --> 00:11:23,400
So listen, Boraqchin,

187
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:25,690
do you remember
what you had said to me?

188
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,530
"To ensure the Mongols
are not divided,

189
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:31,320
and to ensure
our hearts remain as one."

190
00:11:32,070 --> 00:11:33,910
You said I should take action.

191
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:38,000
Tell me, have I let you down?

192
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:43,500
[BORAQCHIN] Möge, you're fine
just the way you are.

193
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:46,290
As honest and as kind as ever.

194
00:11:46,380 --> 00:11:47,920
But what does that all mean?

195
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:51,170
Don't you worry about a thing.

196
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:56,050
If you say so, Boraqchin.

197
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:00,430
♪

198
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,520
[BORAQCHIN] Möge...

199
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:03,560
you don't need
to concern yourself

200
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:05,020
with any of this.

201
00:12:05,110 --> 00:12:08,150
This is a wager
that I've thrown myself into

202
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:09,780
completely on my own.

203
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:13,950
[Ögedei chuckles]

204
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:17,370
[BORAQCHIN] I apologize
for the wait, Great Kha'an.

205
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:20,040
There's something
you wished to discuss?

206
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:22,710
Yes, I have a proposal.

207
00:12:22,790 --> 00:12:24,630
It is about that woman.

208
00:12:24,710 --> 00:12:27,420
Tolui's widow,
Sorghaghtani Beki.

209
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:30,630
-[QADAQ] Get out of here.
-[SITARA] I won't.

210
00:12:30,710 --> 00:12:32,630
Please, leave us!

211
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,550
I won't! I'm sorry!

212
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:35,510
[Güyük trembling]

213
00:12:35,970 --> 00:12:38,300
I know that you want
to help Lady Töregene.

214
00:12:38,390 --> 00:12:40,100
Today is not the day.

215
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,270
I see.

216
00:12:42,430 --> 00:12:43,480
-[gasps]
-Uh?

217
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,850
[grunts] Wait!

218
00:12:45,350 --> 00:12:48,570
Prince Güyük! Your mother
also means a great deal to me.

219
00:12:48,650 --> 00:12:51,030
Please. If there's
anything you can tell me,

220
00:12:51,110 --> 00:12:52,570
for her sake, you must.

221
00:12:52,650 --> 00:12:53,610
[Güyük trembles]

222
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:54,990
-[SHIRA] Hey.
-[BOTH] Uh?

223
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:57,200
So, someone's coming.

224
00:12:59,410 --> 00:13:00,540
Hey!

225
00:13:00,620 --> 00:13:01,660
[Sitara gasps]

226
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:03,210
I've seen that woman.

227
00:13:03,290 --> 00:13:05,160
She serves under
Empress Boraqchin.

228
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:06,330
No matter what,

229
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:08,040
we can't let her find out
we're here.

230
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:09,250
[SHIRA] What do we do?

231
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,920
[SITARA] Good question.

232
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:14,970
[ALL] She's here now!
She's here now!

233
00:13:15,550 --> 00:13:16,550
♪

234
00:13:18,930 --> 00:13:20,970
[Güyük groans]

235
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:22,140
♪

236
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,360
[LADY-IN-WAITING] Hm.

237
00:13:34,530 --> 00:13:37,910
Mm... A good day to you,
Prince Güyük.

238
00:13:37,990 --> 00:13:39,490
And you, Sir Qadaq.

239
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:42,490
[QADAQ] I trust
Lady Töregene's safe and sound?

240
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:44,040
[LADY-IN-WAITING] Of course.

241
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,580
In fact, I've come to inform you

242
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,080
that they're all ready
to release her.

243
00:13:47,170 --> 00:13:48,210
[both gasp]

244
00:13:48,290 --> 00:13:49,880
-[LADY-IN-WAITING] Mm?
-[QADAQ] Huh?

245
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,550
[Qadaq groans, sneezes]

246
00:13:52,630 --> 00:13:54,340
Sorry, continue.

247
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:55,840
Right.

248
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:58,760
There are a number
of conditions, however.

249
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,300
[SITARA] Conditions?

250
00:14:00,390 --> 00:14:01,550
[LADY-IN-WAITING]
First, Lady Töregene

251
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,970
appears quite weary.

252
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,810
She will spend her time quietly

253
00:14:04,890 --> 00:14:07,190
in Prince Güyük's territory
from now on.

254
00:14:07,270 --> 00:14:08,690
[SITARA]
So they don't want her returning

255
00:14:08,770 --> 00:14:09,730
to the emperor's court?

256
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:12,070
[LADY-IN-WAITING]
And there's one more thing.

257
00:14:12,150 --> 00:14:15,190
As a final stipulation
of her being released,

258
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:18,150
the prince must marry
Princess Sorghaghtani.

259
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,450
[gasps]

260
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:26,040
All right,
we understand your conditions.

261
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:28,290
But we need to think it over.

262
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:32,090
Do think carefully
about what's best for her.

263
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:34,460
And for all of the Mongols
as well.

264
00:14:35,130 --> 00:14:37,050
With that, I must go.

265
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:41,050
[Güyük trembling]

266
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:42,300
[sighs]

267
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:44,180
I'd say you held out quite well.

268
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:46,020
-Uh...
-[SITARA] Excuse me.

269
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:48,600
About what she just said...

270
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:50,730
[Qadaq groans]

271
00:14:50,810 --> 00:14:51,810
[SHIRA] Uh...

272
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:53,650
[birds squawking]

273
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:55,150
So, in other words,

274
00:14:55,230 --> 00:14:58,030
all of this is a part
of the Great Khatun's plot.

275
00:14:58,110 --> 00:15:01,070
Her main goal is to weaken
the House of Tolui.

276
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:04,160
And then vest the Great Kha'an
with more authority.

277
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:06,540
To accomplish this,

278
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:09,370
she needed Prince Tolui
to not simply perish,

279
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:11,500
but to look like
he sacrificed himself

280
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:12,630
for the Great Kha'an.

281
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:14,090
[Boraqchin chuckles softly]

282
00:15:14,170 --> 00:15:17,050
That means
the Great Kha'an's ailment was--

283
00:15:17,130 --> 00:15:20,090
Yes. She used Lady Töregene
in her scheme

284
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:21,260
to give him poison.

285
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:22,760
One that wouldn't
quite kill him.

286
00:15:22,850 --> 00:15:24,550
[SITARA] Rahj al-gar.

287
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,470
To carry out her plan,

288
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,930
she tested the poison
on herself.

289
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,100
[Ögedei breathes uneasily]

290
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,060
[SITARA]
Using alchemy to orchestrate

291
00:15:32,150 --> 00:15:33,980
people's lives and deaths.

292
00:15:34,770 --> 00:15:36,480
As a witch would.

293
00:15:37,990 --> 00:15:40,900
[QADAQ] And she's even gotten
Prince Güyük involved in this...

294
00:15:40,990 --> 00:15:42,950
making him marry the princess.

295
00:15:43,030 --> 00:15:44,740
[SHIRA]
Nothing to object to, right?

296
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:47,580
Seems like it's the only way to
bring Lady Töregene back to us.

297
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:50,540
[Qadaq sighs]

298
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:53,210
Well, that is true.

299
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,540
Yes, but still...

300
00:15:56,090 --> 00:15:57,340
-[SITARA] Prince Güyük!
-Uh?

301
00:15:57,420 --> 00:16:00,590
Oh, please, please rescue
Lady Töregene.

302
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:02,010
I beg of you!

303
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,340
[GÜYÜK] Hmm.

304
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:06,350
[breathes nervously]

305
00:16:07,470 --> 00:16:08,560
[sighs]

306
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:11,180
-[GÜYÜK] I'll do it.
-[Sitara exclaims]

307
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,150
[bleating]

308
00:16:15,060 --> 00:16:18,520
So long. I should be returning
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

309
00:16:18,610 --> 00:16:19,820
-Hold on.
-Uh?

310
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:22,650
You cannot tell anyone
what we talked about.

311
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:25,620
[SHIRA] Understood. [chuckles]

312
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:27,490
I sure hope so.

313
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,240
You must feel so relieved.

314
00:16:29,330 --> 00:16:30,580
[grunts]

315
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:32,960
Now you'll be able
to save the one you wanted to.

316
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,790
Thank you, Shira.

317
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:40,920
It was reassuring
having you here with me.

318
00:16:41,550 --> 00:16:43,590
Um, right, uh, I'm glad.

319
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,300
[chuckles]

320
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:48,510
Goodbye.
And may Allah preserve you.

321
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,140
Make sure you keep the secret.

322
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:51,680
Sure, sure.

323
00:16:56,690 --> 00:16:58,150
[HULEGU] What's that?

324
00:16:58,230 --> 00:17:01,230
My mother? Marry Güyük?
Not a chance!

325
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,320
Yes.

326
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:04,650
That is what the Great Khatun's
messenger was telling me.

327
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:06,530
It is clear to me
the House of Ögedei

328
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:08,080
has dropped all pretense.

329
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,620
The lowly son
of the sixth empress

330
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,870
is completely unfit
to marry her.

331
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:15,540
That may be, but it is what
the Great Khatun wishes.

332
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:16,790
♪

333
00:17:18,250 --> 00:17:19,380
[SORGHAGHTANI] I see.

334
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:22,760
[HULEGU] Mother,
you won't accept this, will you?

335
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:25,930
I refuse to ever call Güyük
my "father."

336
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:30,640
Mother? Mother? [stutters]

337
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:31,850
Mother!

338
00:17:31,930 --> 00:17:34,430
[Shira sighs]
She seems pretty spiritless.

339
00:17:35,060 --> 00:17:36,350
Maybe it would've helped

340
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,770
if I mentioned
who killed Prince Tolui, too.

341
00:17:40,230 --> 00:17:42,440
I never thought
Princess Sorghaghtani

342
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:43,650
would remarry.

343
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:46,030
Mm. In the near future,

344
00:17:46,110 --> 00:17:48,490
our two houses
will further join hands.

345
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:50,620
I was about to send a messenger

346
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:53,120
to go and speak
with the princess.

347
00:17:53,830 --> 00:17:56,750
Well then, in that case,
could you let me have the honor?

348
00:17:57,330 --> 00:17:59,500
-You want to go?
-Yes.

349
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,630
You gave me the book
I've wanted all this time,

350
00:18:02,710 --> 00:18:05,840
which is truly precious
to someone born to scholars.

351
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,550
So, I want to repay
your kindness.

352
00:18:08,630 --> 00:18:09,720
Oh?

353
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:12,100
I'm well-acquainted
with the princess.

354
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:15,390
And I feel certain
I can persuade her without fail.

355
00:18:15,470 --> 00:18:17,810
I see. Intriguing.

356
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:27,650
[SITARA] It's been three years
since last we spoke.

357
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:31,240
That is the role of someone
who will be empress one day.

358
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:34,910
[SITARA] Now that the princess
has been reduced to this,

359
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:38,210
how will she react
when she sees me again?

360
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:40,000
Will she be angry?

361
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:41,460
Will she start yelling?

362
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:44,340
That's fine by me.

363
00:18:45,050 --> 00:18:48,470
The anger I feel towards her
burns far more intensely

364
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:50,180
than she could imagine.

365
00:18:52,050 --> 00:18:53,100
Pardon me.

366
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:56,020
[SORGHAGHTANI] Fatima?

367
00:18:56,430 --> 00:18:58,020
It's been so long.

368
00:18:58,100 --> 00:19:01,650
Yes, I've been away
for quite some time now.

369
00:19:01,730 --> 00:19:04,650
Please forgive me.
You see, I... [gasps]

370
00:19:06,570 --> 00:19:07,990
♪

371
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:13,160
Shira did tell me that
she was terribly despondent.

372
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:19,000
I am here today as a messenger
for the Great Khatun.

373
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:22,580
I'm sorry for the loss
of your husband.

374
00:19:22,670 --> 00:19:24,540
I wish there was something
I could have done.

375
00:19:24,630 --> 00:19:25,920
-It's all right.
-Mm?

376
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:27,710
♪

377
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:33,100
Please take a look at this.

378
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,930
It's a fine gift
from the Great Khatun.

379
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,100
Also...

380
00:19:38,640 --> 00:19:41,940
I've come to discuss a matter
of great consequence.

381
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,060
One that will affect us all.

382
00:19:45,110 --> 00:19:47,030
Please do not be alarmed.

383
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,320
But I was sent here
because she asks

384
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:50,690
that you marry Prince Güyük--

385
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:52,700
-I'll do as she says.
-Uh?

386
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:54,450
Huh?

387
00:19:54,910 --> 00:19:57,580
[SORGHAGHTANI] If it will serve
the Mongol people in any way,

388
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:01,080
then do with me as you see fit.

389
00:20:02,250 --> 00:20:04,420
[SITARA] What?
You can't be serious.

390
00:20:05,250 --> 00:20:06,500
[gasps]

391
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:09,300
Impossible.

392
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:13,180
You, who robbed me
of everyone I loved...

393
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:14,430
♪

394
00:20:16,430 --> 00:20:17,720
[indistinct chatter]

395
00:20:22,350 --> 00:20:25,230
You, in all your arrogance...

396
00:20:25,310 --> 00:20:28,820
You gave up hope after losing
someone you cared about?

397
00:20:32,150 --> 00:20:33,400
[Sitara breathes shakily]

398
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:37,490
What's wrong?

399
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:39,830
I admire you.

400
00:20:40,370 --> 00:20:42,870
No, I need to look up at her.

401
00:20:43,290 --> 00:20:44,880
I just have to give her a smile,

402
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:47,090
like I always do.

403
00:20:47,670 --> 00:20:48,840
[breathes shakily]

404
00:20:50,510 --> 00:20:52,510
There is no one left
to protect you.

405
00:20:53,510 --> 00:20:55,930
[panting]

406
00:20:58,350 --> 00:21:00,390
If you want to shut down
and yield to her,

407
00:21:00,470 --> 00:21:01,390
then suit yourself.

408
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:07,360
But even though
I've lost the ones

409
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,940
who were truly precious to me,

410
00:21:10,030 --> 00:21:11,900
I'll never give up hope.

411
00:21:11,980 --> 00:21:13,650
[Sorghaghtani gasps]

412
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,700
[SITARA] Stop sulking.

413
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:18,910
I will continue thinking
for myself.

414
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:20,790
♪

415
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:31,460
Now then, the matter
at hand is the remarriage

416
00:21:31,550 --> 00:21:33,880
of Princess Sorghaghtani
to Prince Güyük.

417
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:37,640
Yes, Sorghaghtani Beki
has consented.

418
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:40,600
Do you have any objections,
Prince Güyük?

419
00:21:42,970 --> 00:21:44,060
[sighs]

420
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:50,270
I hope this marriage
forges a new bond

421
00:21:50,360 --> 00:21:52,610
between the Houses
of Ögedei and Tolui.

422
00:21:53,530 --> 00:21:54,820
How heartwarming.

423
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,540
[SITARA]
It was unwise for me

424
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:07,210
to behave as I did with
Princess Sorghaghtani.

425
00:22:08,330 --> 00:22:11,420
Well, I feel certain
we won't ever meet again.

426
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:12,670
♪

427
00:22:15,210 --> 00:22:16,720
[indistinct chatter]

428
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:17,760
[SITARA] Mm?

429
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:19,220
Uh?

430
00:22:21,300 --> 00:22:22,560
[gasps]

431
00:22:30,650 --> 00:22:34,110
Finally, the date of the wedding
ceremony will be set for--

432
00:22:34,190 --> 00:22:35,900
-[SORGHAGHTANI] Wait a moment.
-[BOTH] Uh?

433
00:22:35,990 --> 00:22:37,490
[all exclaim]

434
00:22:39,820 --> 00:22:42,990
I'm afraid
preparations won't be needed.

435
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:45,040
[MAN 1] Wait.
Princess Sorghaghtani!

436
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:46,120
[MAN 2] What does that mean?

437
00:22:46,450 --> 00:22:48,080
-[all gasp]
-[MAN] Why won't they be needed?

438
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:49,540
[gasping]

439
00:22:53,250 --> 00:22:56,590
[SORGHAGHTANI] Sweet Tolui,
I learned what it's like

440
00:22:56,670 --> 00:22:59,720
to lose someone
for the very first time.

441
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:03,140
[Tolui laughs]

442
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:05,600
[SORGHAGHTANI]
And to give up all hope.

443
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:07,890
-[Tolui breathes uneasily]
-[Sorghaghtani cries]

444
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:11,350
[SORGHAGHTANI] Oh, Tolui.

445
00:23:13,270 --> 00:23:15,940
Do you think
this is how she felt?

446
00:23:17,740 --> 00:23:21,740
I hope you'll forgive me,
Great Kha'an and Great Khatun.

447
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,280
But you see...

448
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:27,040
I've chosen to decline
this marriage offer.

449
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:28,160
[Boraqchin grunts]

450
00:23:32,670 --> 00:23:36,630
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next time,
"The Steppe, Ever Unchanging."

